I didn't think this was about realism - more about believable fantasy
and therefore you might try looking at some of the fantasy fiction for
examples of female fighters. I believe Marion Zimmer Bradley has written
about quite a few, some of the dragon riders of Pern are pretty tough
women, etc. Then there is mythology, Diana the huntress for instance.

Funny you should say that archeologists are usually men, but the woman
who had the biggest influence on me as a child (other than my mother) was
a keen amatuer archeologist who still seems to know more about the local
sites than the paid professionals... she was also an auxillary nurse - an
occupation that requires great physical strength!

